      "writtenOn": "2024-01-12T11:12:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Nit: it would be best to explain to developers what the tradeoff is here, and why they shouldn\u0027t use this in general.\n\nBasically: if the TTL is too short, discovery will take more time and be less reliable, as advertised services will quickly expire.\nIf the TTL is too long, when the device loses network connectivity, other devices on the network will take a long time to realize that it has disappeared.\nUnless they have a specific use-case and done extensive testing, developers should not set any explicit TTL with this method.",
      "revId": "a4dbdea9997b7088d52fba01a4a1fe099dee04c8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
